%%%
# Allele-class frequencies: Dirichlet prior, categorical genotypes

Three allele classes with a `Dirichlet` prior on their frequencies `p`;
thirty genotyped individuals are iid `Categorical(p)` draws. The model
is conjugate, so the posterior log-density is closed form. The fixture
scores a SIMPLEX latent inside a `bayesupdate` — the density sweep
scores the bare Dirichlet law only — with the latent vector indexed by
a discrete iid likelihood.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

% Class labels 1 to 3 with class counts 14, 8, 8.
counts_data = [1, 3, 2, 1, 1, 3, 2, 2, 1, 3, 3, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 1, 1, 3, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 1]

p ~ Dirichlet(alpha = [2.0, 3.0, 4.0])
y ~ iid(Categorical(p = p), lengthof(counts_data))

prior = lawof(record(p = p))
forward_kernel = kernelof(record(y = y), p = p)
L = likelihoodof(forward_kernel, record(y = counts_data))
posterior = bayesupdate(L, prior)
